          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "About Organic Snooze",
            "question": "What is Gary Brecka's connection to Ultimate Snooze?",
            "answer": "<p>Gary Brecka partnered with the brand to help create a mattress system aligned with recovery, cleaner sleep, and better daily performance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0005": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "About Organic Snooze",
            "question": "What does clean sleep mean?",
            "answer": "<p>Clean sleep means creating a sleep environment with materials you can understand: organic cotton, organic wool, and natural latex, while avoiding common materials like fiberglass, polyurethane foam, chemical flame retardants, and synthetic adhesives.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0006": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "About Organic Snooze",
            "question": "Why does what my mattress is made of matter?",
            "answer": "<p>You spend nearly one-third of your life on your mattress. The materials closest to your body can affect breathability, comfort, pressure relief, temperature regulation, and the overall cleanliness of your sleep environment.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0007": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "About Organic Snooze",
            "question": "Does Ultimate Snooze use fiberglass or chemical fire retardants?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Ultimate Snooze mattresses are made without fiberglass, chemical flame-retardant sprays, boric acid, or petroleum-based foams. Fire resistance is achieved with a natural wool barrier.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0008": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "About Organic Snooze",
            "question": "Will the mattress have a chemical smell?",
            "answer": "<p>Ultimate Snooze mattresses are made without polyurethane foam comfort layers or chemical adhesives, so they are designed to avoid the strong chemical off-gassing smell associated with many conventional foam mattresses. Natural materials may have a mild natural scent at first.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0009": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "About Organic Snooze",
            "question": "Is Ultimate Snooze HSA/FSA eligible?",
            "answer": "<p>Qualified customers may be eligible to pay with HSA or FSA funds through Truemed. If approved, an independent licensed clinician can issue a Letter of Medical Necessity through Truemed's platform.</p>"
