          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Shipping & Payments",
            "question": "How long does shipping take for a mattress?",
            "answer": "<p>Mattress orders have a processing time of 3-5 business days, followed by 10-14 business days for delivery. Orders placed on weekends are processed the next business day.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0140": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Shipping & Payments",
            "question": "How long does shipping take for accessories?",
            "answer": "<p>Accessory orders have a processing time of 1-2 business days, followed by 10-14 business days for delivery. Products may ship in separate packages.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0141": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Shipping & Payments",
            "question": "Do you offer free shipping?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. All items ship free to the contiguous 48 U.S. states. Customers in Alaska and Hawaii are charged a different shipping rate.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0142": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Shipping & Payments",
            "question": "Do you ship to all 50 U.S. states?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Ultimate Snooze ships within the United States, including Alaska and Hawaii. Customers in Alaska and Hawaii are charged a different shipping rate.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0143": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Shipping & Payments",
            "question": "Do you offer international shipping?",
            "answer": "<p>International shipping is not yet available but is coming soon. Currently, all orders ship within the United States only.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0144": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Shipping & Payments",
            "question": "What payment methods do you accept?",
            "answer": "<p>Ultimate Snooze accepts all major credit cards, Affirm, Shop Pay installments, ACIMA lease-to-own, and HSA/FSA funds through Truemed for qualified purchases.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0145": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Shipping & Payments",
            "question": "Can I track my order?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Once your order ships, you will receive a tracking number by email. For order questions, contact orders@theultimatesnooze.com.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0146": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Shipping & Payments",
            "question": "What is white glove delivery and how much does it cost?",
            "answer": "<p>White glove delivery is a paid add-on handled by LoadUp. Your mattress ships separately by UPS or FedEx, then LoadUp arrives on your scheduled date to help with setup and old mattress removal upon request.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0147": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Shipping & Payments",
            "question": "Can I change my order after placing it?",
            "answer": "<p>You have 24 hours from the time of purchase to modify or cancel your order. Call or text 719-751-6070 with your order number and requested change.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0148": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Shipping & Payments",
            "question": "Do mattresses arrive compressed in a box?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Mattresses arrive compressed and boxed for easier transport through doorways and stairways. A team lift is recommended. The mattress typically expands within 4-8 hours.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0149": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Returns & Trial",
            "question": "How long is the Ultimate Snooze sleep trial?",
            "answer": "<p>Ultimate Snooze offers a 100-night sleep trial.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0150": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Returns & Trial",
            "question": "What is the 30-night break-in period?",
            "answer": "<p>Because natural materials need time to settle and your body needs time to adjust, Ultimate Snooze asks customers to sleep on the mattress for 30 nights before starting a return. The official trial window opens on night 31 and runs through night 100.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0151": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Returns & Trial",
            "question": "How do I start a return?",
            "answer": "<p>Log into your account and complete the return request form. The team typically responds within 1 business day to coordinate next steps.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0152": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Returns & Trial",
            "question": "Do I have to pay to return my mattress?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. There is a $199 return processing fee that covers freight, handling, and responsible removal. If you choose store credit instead of a cash refund, this fee is waived.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0153": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Returns & Trial",
            "question": "What happens to the mattress after I return it?",
            "answer": "<p>Approved returns are coordinated through a local pickup or donation partner where available. Ultimate Snooze works to responsibly rehome or recycle returned mattresses.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0154": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Returns & Trial",
            "question": "Can I return accessories like pillows and sheets?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, within 30 days of delivery. Unopened and sealed accessories have no restocking fee, but the customer pays return shipping. Opened or lightly used items may have a 20% restocking fee.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0155": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Returns & Trial",
            "question": "What condition does the mattress need to be in for a return?",
            "answer": "<p>The mattress must be clean and sanitary, free from stains, odors, pet damage, burns, or structural damage. The law tag must remain attached and untampered.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0156": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Returns & Trial",
            "question": "Can I exchange my mattress for a different size or model?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Mattress exchanges are free. If you upgrade, you pay the price difference. If you downgrade, the difference is issued as store credit valid for 12 months. An exchange does not restart the trial.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0157": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Returns & Trial",
            "question": "When will I receive my refund?",
            "answer": "<p>Refunds are processed within 3-5 business days after the returned mattress is received and inspected. Refunds go to the original payment method.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0158": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Returns & Trial",
            "question": "Is there a restocking fee?",
            "answer": "<p>For mattresses, there is a $199 return processing fee, waived if you choose store credit. Opened or used accessories may have a 20% restocking fee. Adjustable bases are final sale.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0159": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Warranty",
            "question": "How long is the Ultimate Snooze mattress warranty?",
            "answer": "<p>Ultimate Snooze mattresses include a 30-year limited warranty.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0160": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Warranty",
            "question": "What is covered under the 30-year warranty?",
            "answer": "<p>Coverage includes qualifying defects such as sagging greater than 1.5 inches not caused by improper foundation, manufacturing defects, broken or loose coils, faulty tufting or stitching, premature material breakdown, and cover defects such as seam or zipper failure.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0161": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Warranty",
            "question": "What is not covered by the warranty?",
            "answer": "<p>The warranty does not cover normal softening of latex or wool over time, misuse or abuse, stains or spills, mold or mildew from moisture, damage caused by an improper foundation, or normal wear from everyday use.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0162": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Warranty",
            "question": "What is the difference between prorated and non-prorated warranty coverage?",
            "answer": "<p>Years 1-20 are non-prorated. If there is a qualifying defect, Ultimate Snooze will repair or replace the mattress at no cost. Years 21-30 are prorated and provide partial credit toward replacement based on remaining years.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0163": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Warranty",
            "question": "How do I make a warranty claim?",
            "answer": "<p>Contact the Sleep Concierge Team and provide photos or a short video of the issue. The team will review within 3-5 business days and repair or replace the product if the issue qualifies.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0164": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Warranty",
            "question": "Does using an improper foundation void the warranty?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Damage caused by improper foundations, old sagging box springs, or unsupported frames is not covered.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0165": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Warranty",
            "question": "Is the warranty transferable if I sell the mattress?",
            "answer": "<p>No. The warranty is non-transferable. Claims require proof of purchase directly from Ultimate Snooze.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0166": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Warranty",
            "question": "Does the warranty cover natural softening of the latex?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Normal softening of latex or wool over time is considered expected comfort settling and is not covered unless it meets the defined defect threshold.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0167": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Warranty",
            "question": "What foundation types are required to keep the warranty valid?",
            "answer": "<p>Use a platform bed with a flat sturdy surface, a slatted foundation with slats no more than 3 inches apart, or a compatible adjustable base.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0168": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Warranty",
            "question": "Are accessories like pillows and sheets covered by warranty?",
            "answer": "<p>Accessories such as pillows, sheets, protectors, and toppers do not carry the mattress warranty. Accessories are covered by the applicable return window. Adjustable bases carry a separate 20-year warranty.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0169": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "HSA/FSA",
            "question": "Can I use HSA or FSA funds to buy a mattress?",
            "answer": "<p>Qualified customers may be able to use HSA or FSA funds through Truemed. Eligibility depends on your health plan and approval through the Truemed process.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0170": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "HSA/FSA",
            "question": "What is Truemed?",
            "answer": "<p>Truemed is a partner platform that helps eligible customers use HSA/FSA funds for qualified wellness-related purchases by connecting them with an independent licensed clinician for eligibility review.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0171": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "HSA/FSA",
            "question": "Do I need a Letter of Medical Necessity?",
            "answer": "<p>In many cases, HSA/FSA use requires a Letter of Medical Necessity. If approved, Truemed's platform can help facilitate this through an independent licensed clinician.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0172": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "HSA/FSA",
            "question": "Can I use my HSA/FSA card at checkout?",
            "answer": "<p>If approved through Truemed and supported by your plan, you may be able to use HSA/FSA funds for qualifying products. Follow the checkout prompts or Truemed eligibility flow for instructions.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0173": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "HSA/FSA",
            "question": "Is HSA/FSA approval guaranteed?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Approval depends on your individual health plan, eligibility, and Truemed's review process.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0174": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "HSA/FSA",
            "question": "Can I use HSA/FSA for pillows or bedding?",
            "answer": "<p>Eligibility varies by product and plan. Truemed can help determine which products may qualify.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0175": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "HSA/FSA",
            "question": "Can I use HSA/FSA with financing?",
            "answer": "<p>Eligibility and payment structure may vary by plan and checkout method. Confirm through Truemed and your HSA/FSA provider before purchase.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0176": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "HSA/FSA",
            "question": "What happens if I am not approved for HSA/FSA eligibility?",
            "answer": "<p>If you are not approved, you can still purchase using another accepted payment method such as credit card, Affirm, Shop Pay installments, or ACIMA.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0177": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Compare Mattresses",
            "question": "Organic latex vs memory foam: what is the difference?",
            "answer": "<p>Memory foam has a slow-sinking feel and can trap heat. Natural latex is more responsive, breathable, and buoyant while still offering pressure relief.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0178": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Compare Mattresses",
            "question": "Organic mattress vs regular mattress: what is the difference?",
            "answer": "<p>A regular mattress may use synthetic foams, fiberglass, chemical flame retardants, or adhesives. An organic mattress focuses on natural and organic materials such as cotton, wool, and latex.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0179": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Compare Mattresses",
            "question": "Latex mattress vs hybrid mattress: which is better?",
            "answer": "<p>A latex hybrid combines latex comfort layers with supportive coils. This gives you the pressure relief and breathability of latex with the support and airflow of coils.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0180": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Compare Mattresses",
            "question": "Pillowtop vs firm mattress: which should I choose?",
            "answer": "<p>Choose the Pillowtop if you want more pressure relief and a cushion-firm feel. Choose the Pure if you want firmer, flatter support.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0181": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Compare Mattresses",
            "question": "Pure Organic vs Pillowtop: which mattress is right for me?",
            "answer": "<p>The Pure is best for firmer support and a simpler comfort profile. The Pillowtop is best for sleepers who want more pressure relief, a taller profile, and a more luxury comfort feel.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0182": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Compare Mattresses",
            "question": "Latex topper vs memory foam topper: which is better?",
            "answer": "<p>A latex topper is more responsive and breathable, while memory foam is slower-sinking and may retain more heat. Latex is a strong choice for people who want pressure relief without feeling stuck.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0183": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Compare Mattresses",
            "question": "Organic cotton sheets vs bamboo sheets: which is better?",
            "answer": "<p>Organic cotton is natural, breathable, and familiar in feel. Bamboo sheets are often marketed as cooling, but many are heavily processed. Customers seeking a more natural sleep system often choose organic cotton or linen.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_0184": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "tab_label": "Compare Mattresses",
            "question": "Linen sheets vs cotton sheets: which sleeps cooler?",
            "answer": "<p>Linen generally sleeps cooler and more breathable, while cotton is softer and smoother from the start. Linen-cotton blends offer a balance of cooling and softness.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
